## Why MenuRAM

- Running local models on an **18GB** Apple Silicon Mac.
- Thought loading the model meant enough RAM. **KV cache** used the rest.
- First tool: **Ollama**. Outputs kept getting truncated. Raised context window. Did not notice the real issue at first.
- Mac got very slow. Activity Monitor: memory basically full, **heavy swap**.
- Checking RAM meant opening Activity Monitor, clicking the Memory tab, waiting a few seconds for totals. Bad glance UX.
- Built a **menu bar extra**: used / total always visible; click for available, pressure, swap, top apps.
- Status: still in development, running from **Xcode**, used daily, genuinely helpful. No App Store / notarized build yet. No public users yet, so no user-count on the card.
- Repo: https://github.com/hjo3-cse40/MenuRAM
- LinkedIn launch: https://www.linkedin.com/feed/update/urn:li:activity:7496666525068636160/
- Honest claim: MenuRAM shows load (pressure/swap) before the next run. It does **not** fix truncation. Truncation was small default context windows. Raising context grew KV cache and then swap.

## Local model notes (separate post)

- Started with **Gemma 4 12B** via Ollama. That is when truncation / RAM pain showed up.
- Ollama app UI was too simple: hard to set thinking on/off or effort levels, and to control context window.
- Switched to **LM Studio**. More control. Using it now.
- Models under test (said “Kuen”; treat as **Qwen** unless he confirms the exact card): **Qwen 2.7 8B Instruct** and **Llama 3.1 8B Instruct**.
- Gave them tougher edge-case eval questions (full prompt set later).
- Early take: Qwen is more methodical, follows instructions better, more calculated. Llama 3.1 8B strengths still unclear. Keep experimenting.
